00:22:39,420 --> 00:22:44,300
what are the actions that are available to you depending on the states you're in.

279
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:52,460
So it only looks forward. And so the Markov decision process basically has a state and has

280
00:22:52,460 --> 00:22:59,420
a set of actions and you get the reward functions by taking one action depending on one state.

281
00:23:00,460 --> 00:23:08,140
You get discount factor which basically says how important the future is

282
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:13,860
And then you get the transition functions that tell you, well, if I was in one state

283
00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:18,500
and I took one action, what is the next state I'm in, basically.

284
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:24,820
And the goal of the MDP is to find a policy that basically maximizes the cumulative reward

285
00:23:24,820 --> 00:23:25,900
along the future.

286
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:30,540
So the real function is this one.

